# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FinEdge Loan – Frontend Environment Configuration
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Backend URL used by Next.js server-side rewrites (next.config.mjs).
# The browser never talks to this URL directly — it calls same-origin
# "/api/*", and Next.js proxies that server-side to BACKEND_URL. This is
# the ONE variable you must set after deploying the backend.
#
# Local dev: leave unset (defaults to http://localhost:8000)
# Production (Vercel dashboard → Project Settings → Environment Variables):
#   BACKEND_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com
# Must be set BEFORE the Vercel build — next.config.mjs reads it at build time.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# NOT CURRENTLY USED — no code reads process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL.
# frontend/lib/api.ts and frontend/app/negotiate/page.tsx hardcode the
# literal string "/api" directly instead. Kept here for documentation only;
# changing this value has no effect unless the code is updated to read it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/api
